%language Git rebase

# A command on a commit is a keyword, the commit a builtin, its subject a
# comment, which has no effect on the rebase
> pick a1b2c3d Fix the parser
  ^^^^ keyword
       ^^^^^^^ constant.builtin
               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment
> s 8b9c0d1 fixup! Add tests
  ^ keyword
    ^^^^^^^ constant.builtin
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment

# A fixup is an attribute, with `-C` too, and its subject a comment
> fixup 2e3f4a5 Tidy up
  ^^^^^ attribute
                ^^^^^^^ comment
> fixup -C 2e3f4a5 Tidy up
  ^^^^^ attribute
           ^^^^^^^ constant.builtin
                   ^^^^ comment
                        ^^ comment

# A label is made and used; a merge names a commit, a label and its
# message
> label onto
  ^^^^^ function
        ^^^^ constant
> merge -C 1a2b3c4 onto # Merge branch
  ^^^^^ keyword
           ^^^^^^^ constant.builtin
                   ^^^^ constant
                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string

# What `exec` runs is Shell
> exec cargo test --all
  ^^^^ keyword
       ^^^^^ function
                  ^^^^^ constant
> x echo "done"
  ^ keyword
    ^^^^ function.builtin
         ^^^^^^ string

# git's comments
> # Rebase 1a2b3c4..6b7c8d9 onto 1a2b3c4 (8 commands)
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ comment
